From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] flow: AUTO_MEMORIES_JSON, where AUTO_MEMORIES' inventory is
 written
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Before, gen_memories.py always wrote the inventory to
$(RESULTS_DIR)/memories.json, and make's chain named that path. A build
that runs the whole design's detection only to check another source of
the memories against it (bazel-orfs builds a design's memories from the
union of its Verilog slices) had to move the file aside after make, and
the moved-from path is the same one the union is declared at.

Now AUTO_MEMORIES_JSON names the file, with an overridable default:

  export AUTO_MEMORIES_JSON ?= $(RESULTS_DIR)/memories.json

gen_memories.py --json and the make chain (yosys-dependencies,
canonicalize, klayout.lyt) go through it. With the default nothing
changes.

Carried in bazel-orfs, on 0214 (AUTO_MEMORIES_DIR). Not upstreamed;
an upstream candidate beside ORFS #4824. Retires at a bump onto an ORFS
that carries it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
